implementationPlan.description:
ADVERSARIAL REVIEW AND RESTORED MUTATION DRILLS. Review first: what happens if two releases run concurrently over one attempt and both see ABSENT (both then call the producer — the loser must still refuse under the producer's code, not crash); null/malformed `bound.projectId` or `durable.attempt.attemptId` (the lookup answers QUERY_MALFORMED, which must now travel out as a lookup-layer refusal rather than reaching the producer); a store whose horizon read throws mid-scan; whether any arm can silently yield zero cases; and whether the refusal provenance is exact at every hop.

BEFORE MUTATING, run `git status --porcelain --` on each exact path you are about to mutate. `apps/daemon/src/work/attempt-release-boundary.test.ts` is NEW and therefore UNTRACKED (`??`), so `git diff` over it is EMPTY before, during and after a mutation and certifies NOTHING: back it up to %TEMP% suffixed by your worker id and prove its restoration by SHA256 equality in a call SEPARATE from the restore. Tracked paths prove restoration with an empty exact-path `git diff --exit-code`.

Drills, one degree of freedom at a time, restored separately after each:
(a) delete the new lookup-first block in `deriveSafeBoundary` — ARM A's exactly-one-row assertion must red, AND the three consumer arms must red again with their step-1 messages;
(b) change the ABSENT test so EVERY lookup refusal is carried instead of only non-ABSENT — ARM C1's 0 -> 1 write control must red;
(c) change `carryLookupRefusal`'s `refusedBy` to this module's own layer while leaving the code intact — ARM B1 must red on LAYER specifically, proving it pins the refusing layer and not just the code;
(d) with (a) applied, additionally run the same two-different-commandId scenario routed through `reReadSources` and record that it stays GREEN. That is the documented evidence that the sibling's identical fence masks this guard and that ARM A's direct call is the divergence input the epic rail requires. Do NOT delete the sibling fence to make this drill interesting.

A drill that comes back green where it was expected red is a FINDING to report, not a pass to bank. After all drills, rerun step 5's exact command green with nonzero counts, inspect `git status --porcelain` for changes confined to the declared six paths, and put the drill names and outcomes plus the baseline-vs-HEAD attribution in the completion summary for QA.

